title: "CheckMetadataHash: reject mode 1 for extension versions other than 0"
doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
    description: |
      The RFC-0078 metadata hash only describes the transaction extensions of extension
      version 0. A transaction using another extension version with `mode = 1` signed a hash
      that does not cover its own extensions. `CheckMetadataHash` now rejects such
      transactions with `InvalidTransaction::BadProof` during validation.

      Signed transactions (extrinsic format 4) and general transactions using extension
      version 0 are unaffected. `mode = 0` is unaffected for every extension version.
crates:
  - name: frame-metadata-hash-extension
    bump: patch
